# ── Netlify Redirects — CA Reshma CRM ───────────────────────────────
#
# All API calls go through /api proxy — the real GAS URL is never
# exposed in browser source code. Netlify forwards server-side.
#
# HOW IT WORKS:
#   Frontend calls:  /api?action=client_list
#   Netlify sends:   https://script.google.com/.../exec?action=client_list
#   Browser sees:    only /api — GAS URL is hidden
#
# DEPLOY: put this file in the ROOT of your Netlify site (same folder
# as index.html, ca-workspace.html etc.)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# NOTE (AI chat POC): this GAS proxy rule is not called by anything in this
# repo — ca-workspace.html fetches the GAS URL directly (see APPS_SCRIPT_URL
# in ca-workspace.html), it never fetches through /api/*. It's commented out
# here because Cloudflare Workers Static Assets also parses this
# `_redirects` file (Pages-style), and its wildcard would otherwise match
# and swallow the new same-origin /api/chat* Worker route before the Worker
# ever saw the request. Uncomment only if something starts relying on it —
# and if so, scope it below /api/chat so it doesn't shadow the chat API.
# /api/*  https://script.google.com/macros/s/AKfycbxJdTaL6_6XrJcfFBFkFtp5tV3-vPUAwSnJfQdV1Xx93dJgo4gRmy8a1W0EALDgecn3/exec/:splat  200

